<title>TURKMENISTAN: Turkmens get four U.S. flour mills with storage.</title>
<headline>Turkmens get four U.S. flour mills with storage.</headline>
<dateline>ASHGABAT 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S.-based Ibberson International Incorporated is building four flour mills in the former Soviet republic of Turkmenistan at a cost of $71.3 million, a Turkmen agricultural official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The official said the Minneapolis-based company had already completed $23 million worth of work.</p>
<p>Each of the mills, with a production capacity of 200 tonnes of flour a day, will be able to store 50,000 tonnes of grain.</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom +7 3272 509410</p>
